WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.108
TIMESTAMP stores a date and local clock time It does
not carry a time-zone

00:00:06.122 --> 00:00:12.296
interpretation That can be appropriate when the time
zone is fixed or irrelevant

00:00:14.035 --> 00:00:18.456
But if records come from multiple regions or you
need to compare global instants a

00:00:18.469 --> 00:00:20.627
plain timestamp can become ambiguous
